WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.080 --> 00:00:02.369
Know your rights to rest at work.

2
00:00:02.369 --> 00:00:06.600
These are the legal minimums for adult workers, so save this.

3
00:00:06.780 --> 00:00:13.202
If you work more than 6 hours a day, you have the right to one uninterrupted 20-minute break.

4
00:00:13.202 --> 00:00:15.473
By law, it doesn't have to be paid.

5
00:00:15.473 --> 00:00:16.900
Your contract decides.

6
00:00:17.080 --> 00:00:25.640
Between working days, you get 11 hours' rest, plus 24 hours off each week, or 48 hours each fortnight.

7
00:00:25.640 --> 00:00:31.300
In round-the-clock services like hospitals, you may get compensatory rest instead.

8
00:00:31.480 --> 00:00:35.286
Every year, you get at least 5.6 weeks of paid leave.

9
00:00:35.286 --> 00:00:40.400
That's 28 days for a 5-day week, and your NHS contract may give you more.

10
00:00:40.580 --> 00:00:47.471
Work-life balance is a top topic for our first talk, pencilled in for Sunday 22 November.

11
00:00:47.471 --> 00:00:49.145
What helps you switch off?

12
00:00:49.145 --> 00:00:56.100
Tell us below, and apply to join the Igbo Healthcare Professionals Network, IHPN-UK, at the link in our bio.
